.\" Man page for the History Tracers viewer.
.TH HISTORYTRACERS 1 "2026-09-24" "History Tracers 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
historytracers \- graphical desktop viewer for the History Tracers teaching tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B historytracers
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B historytracers
is the desktop viewer of History Tracers, a free and open-source teaching tool.
.PP
.B This is GUI software.
It is not a command-line or terminal application. When it starts, it opens a
native graphical window and renders the History Tracers content in an embedded
web view (WebView2 on Windows, GTK/WebKit on Linux and the BSDs, and
Cocoa/WebKit on macOS). The options described below only configure that window
and the local content server before the window appears.
.PP
To display the content, the program starts a small HTTP server bound exclusively
to the loopback interface (\fB127.0.0.1\fR) and points the embedded web view to
it. A free port is chosen automatically unless one is set with
.BR \-port .
The server is private to the local machine and stops when the window is closed.
.PP
By default the viewer serves the web content found in the
.I www
directory of the current working directory. Use
.B \-dir
or
.B \-path
to point it to another content directory. When no content is found, a welcome
page is shown instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-port " n"
HTTP port for the local server. Use a value in the range 1\(en65535 to bind a
fixed port, or 0 (the default) to let the program choose a random free port. If
the requested fixed port is unavailable, a random port is chosen instead.
.TP
.BI \-dir " directory"
Content directory to serve (default:
.IR www ).
.TP
.BI \-path " directory"
Content directory to serve. When set, it overrides
.BR \-dir .
.TP
.BI \-lang " code"
Initial interface language, for example
.BR en-US ,
.B pt-BR
or
.BR es-ES .
.TP
.BI \-calendar " name"
Initial calendar used to display dates, for example
.BR gregory ,
.BR julian ,
.BR hebrew ,
.BR islamic ,
.BR persian ,
.BR french ,
.BR shaka ,
.BR hispanic ,
.BR mesoamerican ,
.BR emesoamerican ,
.BR aymara ,
.BR mapuche ,
.BR inca ,
.BR chinese ,
.BR javanese
or
.BR japanese .
.TP
.BI \-class " uuid"
Open the class content with the given UUID when the window opens.
.TP
.BI \-log " file"
Write an HTTP access log to
.IR file .
By default no access log is written.
.TP
.BI \-tls-cert " file"
TLS certificate file. When given together with
.BR \-tls-key ,
the local server uses HTTPS.
.TP
.BI \-tls-key " file"
TLS private key file. It must be given together with
.BR \-tls-cert .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-help
Show a short usage message and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I www/
Default web content directory served when no other directory is given.
.TP
.I ~/.config/HistoryTracers/
Per-user state directory on Unix-like systems (on Windows it is
.IR %USERPROFILE%\\HistoryTracers ).
It stores the saved window options
.RI ( options.bin ),
the browsing history
.RI ( history.csv ),
the favourites
.RI ( favorites.csv )
and the installation identifier
.RI ( uuid.bin ).
.TP
.I /etc/historytracers/historytracers.conf
System configuration file installed by the History Tracers packages.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start the viewer with the default content directory:
.PP
.nf
.RS
historytracers
.RE
.fi
.PP
Use a specific content directory and start in Portuguese:
.PP
.nf
.RS
historytracers \-path /usr/share/historytracers/www \-lang pt\-BR
.RE
.fi
.PP
Serve the content over HTTPS on a fixed port:
.PP
.nf
.RS
historytracers \-port 8443 \-tls\-cert cert.pem \-tls\-key key.pem
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation and the web version of the content:
.IR https://historytracers.org/ .
